C
  ==
  - Strict analogy with Williams' _(1)hw(e/)_
    results in the (non-standard) modern reading hwe1 [hʷɛː].
    However, because Williams' _(1)hw(e/)_ was likely sounded *[hʷeɪ]
    (based on [his description of the final _(e/)_](/intro/#final-order-29)),
    I hypothesise here that _(1)hw(e/)_ actually corresponds to
    the modern interjection wai3, which is sounded [wɐi],
    but liable to be sounded [wei].
  ==
